{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 17,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a dry morsel, and quietness with it, than a house full of sacrifices ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wise servant shall have rule over a son that causeth shame, and shall have part of the inheritance among the brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fining-pot ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for silver, and the furnace for gold: but the LORD trieth the hearts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wicked doer giveth heed to false lips: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a liar giveth ear to a naughty tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that mocketh the poor reproacheth his Maker; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that is glad at calamities shall not be unpunished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Children's children ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the crown of old men; and the glory of children ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their fathers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Excellent speech becometh not a fool: much less do lying lips a prince.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A gift ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a precious stone in the eyes of him that hath it: whithersoever it turneth, it prospereth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that covereth a transgression seeketh love; but he that repeateth a matter separateth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "very",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " friends.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A reproof entereth more into a wise man than a hundred stripes into a fool.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seeketh only rebellion: therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let a bear robbed of her whelps meet a man, rather than a fool in his folly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever rewardeth evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beginning of strife ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " when one letteth out water: therefore withdraw from contention, before it be meddled with.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the just, even they both ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " abomination to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a price in the hand of a fool to get wisdom, seeing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man void of understanding striketh hands, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " becometh surety in the presence of his friend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He loveth transgression that loveth strife: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that exalteth his gate seeketh destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that hath a froward heart findeth no good: and he that hath a perverse tongue falleth into mischief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that begetteth a fool ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "doeth it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his sorrow: and the father of a fool hath no joy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A merry heart doeth good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a medicine: but a broken spirit drieth the bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " taketh a gift out of the bosom to pervert the ways of judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before him that hath understanding; but the eyes of a fool ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the ends of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A foolish son ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a grief to his father, and bitterness to her that bore him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also to punish the just ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not good, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "nor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to strike princes for equity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that hath knowledge spareth his words: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man of understanding is of an excellent spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.17.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even a fool, when he holdeth his peace, is counted wise: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that shutteth his lips ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is esteemed",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man of understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
